{
  "_schema": {
    "description": "Game-default CustomizerData 7-tuple per species. Empirically validated against Primal Heaven (https://primalheaven.com/skin-creator) and Zooming Islander (https://zoomingislander.com/skincreator.html), both public Isle skin editors with in-game-verified output. HDR material values (>1.0) are hue-preserving normalized (scaled so max channel = 1) rather than component-clamped, so bright authored emissive eye colors produce a hue-correct tinted cream instead of pure white.",
    "layer_to_ipc_mapping": {
      "Color1_RedLayer": "male_display",
      "Color2_GreenLayer": "underbelly",
      "Color3_BlueLayer": "flank",
      "Color4_CyanLayer": "body",
      "Color5_MagentaLayer": "markings",
      "Color6_YellowLayer": "detail1"
    },
    "extracted_at": "2026-04-19",
    "remapped_at": "2026-04-20",
    "notes": "Component-clamp turned HDR eye colors into pure (1,1,1) white on 7 species, causing T-Rex etc. to not render fully-black when user picks all-black sliders but leaves the eye picker at palette default. Hue-preserve normalization fixes that: emissive eyes land as tinted cream, visibly distinct from pure white."
